 Root authorization.json must name candidate E033; E020_accepted, E020_server_qualification_pass, independent_source_review_pass and independent_script_review_pass must be true. `prerequisites` contains path/sha256 pairs for E020_acceptance, E020_server_qualification, E033_source_review, E033_script_review and D064_terminal_review. `candidate_sources` contains both repository paths with exact archived path/sha256 records. `evidence_sha256` pins the final scripts-manifest/protocol, source archive and its artifacts, root preparation decision and prerequisite reports. The same immutable authorization hash is supplied to both builds and bound into every binary manifest. No template placeholder grants permission.
 
 A qualifying primary still requires independent audit, original state/menu/resume/F32/GPU controls, exact old/new raw-state and cache lifetime/error/continuation checks, the fixed wide-turn holdout and fresh-original cumulative cohort under later authorization. The feature-only continuation unit must execute in that later qualification; a no-run build does not test it. These conditional packages are not prepared here.
+
+R2 preserves sealed R1 unchanged. The only admission repair excludes two exact pre-existing generated PTX paths from the Git untracked source set and pins their full bytes/size. All other source identity, build, unit, marker, measurement and qualification requirements are unchanged. Authorization belongs in this R2 directory; builds and seven reserved native IDs retain their original unused names.
